# The build context is the repository root. Without this, every image build
# uploads the Windows virtualenv and node_modules — hundreds of MB that the
# Dockerfile then ignores.
.venv/
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/dist-types/
# Build *state*, not just build output. `tsc --build` reads a stale
# tsbuildinfo from the host, concludes the outputs are current, and emits
# nothing — leaving an image whose packages have no `dist/` and a build that
# fails several steps later with "failed to resolve entry for package".
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.git/
.turbo/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.import_linter_cache/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
tests/visual/output/
docs/
